{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-99d61ba80cec3c51", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# A Survey on Audio Diffusion Models: Text To Speech Synthesis and Enhancement in Generative AI\narXiv: 2303.13336\nAuthors: Chenshuang Zhang, Chaoning Zhang, Sheng Zheng, Mengchun Zhang, Maryam Qamar, Sung-Ho Bae, In So Kweon\nYear: 2023 | Venue: \nTopic: \nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Provides the first comprehensive survey specifically focused on recent progress in diffusion-based speech synthesis.\n  2. Categorizes text-to-speech diffusion methods into three distinct groups based on the model stage: acoustic model, vocoder, and end-to-end framework.\n  3. Classifies speech enhancement tasks into two types depending on whether specific signals are removed from or added to the input speech.\n  4. Includes comparisons of experimental results and detailed discussions across the reviewed methods.\n\nTags: TTS/架构-NAR-Diffusion, Vocoder/Diffusion", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "0e9433d4-c325-4618-bb42-c85dd5d271b1", "uuid": "c52827ca-8544-4de0-82d6-5b3ebdf01d1f", "timestamp": "2026-08-14T07:15:50.469Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# A Survey on Audio Diffusion Models: Text To Speech Synthesis and Enhancement in Generative AI\narXiv: 2303.13336\nAuthors: Chenshuang Zhang, Chaoning Zhang, Sheng Zheng, Mengchun Zhang, Maryam Qamar, Sung-Ho Bae, In So Kweon\nYear: 2023 | Venue: \nTopic: \nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Provides the first comprehensive survey specifically focused on recent progress in diffusion-based speech synthesis.\n  2. Categorizes text-to-speech diffusion methods into three distinct groups based on the model stage: acoustic model, vocoder, and end-to-end framework.\n  3. Classifies speech enhancement tasks into two types depending on whether specific signals are removed from or added to the input speech.\n  4. Includes comparisons of experimental results and detailed discussions across the reviewed methods.\n\nTags: TTS/架构-NAR-Diffusion, Vocoder/Diffusion", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-b5806e1c996873e6", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# BridgeVoC: Revitalizing Neural Vocoder from a Restoration Perspective\narXiv: 2511.07116\nAuthors: Andong Li, Tong Lei, Rilin Chen, Kai Li, Meng Yu, Xiaodong Li, Dong Yu, Chengshi Zheng\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: vocoder\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. The vocoder task is reformulated as a specialized audio restoration problem from a data-to-data paradigm, using the range-space spectral surrogate of the Mel-spectrum as the degraded input.\n  2. The Schrödinger bridge framework is introduced to define the stochastic generation trajectory between the range-space spectral surrogate and the target spectrum as dual endpoints.\n  3. A novel subband-aware convolutional diffusion network (BCD) is proposed, utilizing an uneven subband division strategy and large-kernel convolutional-style attention for efficient time-frequency contextual modeling.\n  4. An omnidirectional distillation loss is proposed to enable effective knowledge transfer from the teacher model to the student model for single-step inference by alleviating phase ambiguity.\n  5. Target-related and bijective consistency losses are integrated to further improve the performance of the single-step student model.\n\nTags: Vocoder, Vocoder/Diffusion", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "0e9433d4-c325-4618-bb42-c85dd5d271b1", "uuid": "de3aad79-c043-4ee7-a954-cb76b4557855", "timestamp": "2026-08-14T07:15:50.704Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# BridgeVoC: Revitalizing Neural Vocoder from a Restoration Perspective\narXiv: 2511.07116\nAuthors: Andong Li, Tong Lei, Rilin Chen, Kai Li, Meng Yu, Xiaodong Li, Dong Yu, Chengshi Zheng\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: vocoder\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. The vocoder task is reformulated as a specialized audio restoration problem from a data-to-data paradigm, using the range-space spectral surrogate of the Mel-spectrum as the degraded input.\n  2. The Schrödinger bridge framework is introduced to define the stochastic generation trajectory between the range-space spectral surrogate and the target spectrum as dual endpoints.\n  3. A novel subband-aware convolutional diffusion network (BCD) is proposed, utilizing an uneven subband division strategy and large-kernel convolutional-style attention for efficient time-frequency contextual modeling.\n  4. An omnidirectional distillation loss is proposed to enable effective knowledge transfer from the teacher model to the student model for single-step inference by alleviating phase ambiguity.\n  5. Target-related and bijective consistency losses are integrated to further improve the performance of the single-step student model.\n\nTags: Vocoder, Vocoder/Diffusion", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
