{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-b348ce002bcde912", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# TaDiCodec: Text-aware Diffusion Speech Tokenizer for Speech Language Modeling\narXiv: 2508.16790\nAuthors: Yuancheng Wang, Dekun Chen, Xueyao Zhang, Junan Zhang, Jiaqi Li, Zhizheng Wu\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: codec_vae\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We propose TaDiCodec, a novel speech tokenizer achieving a 6.25 Hz token rate and 0.0875 kbps bitrate via an end-to-end diffusion autoencoder that jointly performs quantization and reconstruction without adversarial training, external pretrained models, or multi-stage training.\n  2. We introduce text-aware and prompt-guided decoding into the diffusion process to facilitate extreme compression and enhance reconstruction quality, ensuring high intelligibility, speaker similarity, and speech quality at ultra-low token rates.\n  3. We validate TaDiCodec by building zero-shot TTS models under both autoregressive and masked language modeling settings, achieving state-of-the-art WERs on challenging benchmarks and supporting efficient real-time inference.\n\nTags: 压缩, 压缩/量化-VAE, 压缩/语义声学-语义, TTS, TTS/架构-AR-LLM, TTS/架构-NAR-Diffusion", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "0e9433d4-c325-4618-bb42-c85dd5d271b1", "uuid": "bf4427ee-18df-4420-90a8-b095ab4d8e78", "timestamp": "2026-08-14T07:16:12.628Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# TaDiCodec: Text-aware Diffusion Speech Tokenizer for Speech Language Modeling\narXiv: 2508.16790\nAuthors: Yuancheng Wang, Dekun Chen, Xueyao Zhang, Junan Zhang, Jiaqi Li, Zhizheng Wu\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: codec_vae\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We propose TaDiCodec, a novel speech tokenizer achieving a 6.25 Hz token rate and 0.0875 kbps bitrate via an end-to-end diffusion autoencoder that jointly performs quantization and reconstruction without adversarial training, external pretrained models, or multi-stage training.\n  2. We introduce text-aware and prompt-guided decoding into the diffusion process to facilitate extreme compression and enhance reconstruction quality, ensuring high intelligibility, speaker similarity, and speech quality at ultra-low token rates.\n  3. We validate TaDiCodec by building zero-shot TTS models under both autoregressive and masked language modeling settings, achieving state-of-the-art WERs on challenging benchmarks and supporting efficient real-time inference.\n\nTags: 压缩, 压缩/量化-VAE, 压缩/语义声学-语义, TTS, TTS/架构-AR-LLM, TTS/架构-NAR-Diffusion", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
